RustFish
========

RustFish is a Rust port of the Stockfish chess engine and is a derivative work
of Stockfish. It is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
(see the LICENSE file).

Stockfish
---------
Stockfish, a UCI chess playing engine derived from Glaurung 2.1
Copyright (C) 2004-2026 The Stockfish developers (see the AUTHORS file in the
upstream repository)

Upstream project:  https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish
Upstream license:  GNU General Public License v3.0 or later

The search algorithm, move ordering, history heuristics, time management,
NNUE architecture and feature sets, and UCI behavior implemented in RustFish
are ports of the corresponding Stockfish C++ code. Credit for their design
belongs to the Stockfish developers and the wider computer chess community.

NNUE network
------------
The embedded neural network file (nn-bddd9d57eb87.nnue) is the official
Stockfish network, trained and distributed by the Stockfish project and
licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0. Network training data and
tooling are credited to the Stockfish project and the Leela Chess Zero
project, whose data is used in Stockfish network training.

Syzygy tablebases
-----------------
The Syzygy tablebase prober is a port of the Stockfish/Pyrrhic-derived probing
code (originally by Ronald de Man, with contributions from Stockfish developers
and the Pyrrhic project by Andrew Grant). Syzygy tablebase files themselves are
not distributed with RustFish.

Tools used for testing
----------------------
- fastchess (Disservin) - https://github.com/Disservin/fastchess (MIT)
- python-chess (Niklas Fiekas) - https://github.com/niklasf/python-chess (GPL-3.0+)

The fastchess binary and sources are used only for testing and are not part of
this repository or its releases.

Please verify the exact years and wording of upstream copyright notices
